    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d536">

                <pb facs="0757" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/4–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Mr. Myron C. Taylor, Personal
                        Representative of President Roosevelt to Pope
                            Pius XII
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-06T15:00:00-04:00">April 6, 1945—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. From the President for Ambassador Taylor only.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“While fully appreciating the high purpose which motivated the suggestion in
                        your no. 73 of April 5,<anchor n="90" xml:id="d536-f1"/> I must disapprove
                        any idea of your going to Paris for purpose indicated. In present
                        circumstances I feel that you should refuse absolutely to accept or listen
                        to any approaches. The danger of misinterpretation by the enemy of our
                        position on unconditional surrender is too great, and I must, therefore,
                        request you to abstain from any further discussions on this subject with the
                        Vatican. With best personal regards.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d536-f1" n="90" xml:id="d536-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. In this telegram to President Roosevelt, Mr. Taylor inquired
                    whether: “preparatory to possible approach of peace through His Holiness would
                    it not be wise procedure in case actual proposal is made for me to secretly and
                    at once to visit Eisenhower in person at Paris headquarters.”
                    (740.00119–EW/4–545)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
